-          "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "Input a real active column $x\\in\\mathbb F^r$ and trailing block $B\\in\\mathbb F^{r\\times q}$, with entries in the floating-point system, $r\\ge1$, and $q\\ge0$. If $x=0$, return the identity action and copy $B$. Otherwise let $s=\\max_i|x_i|>0$, compute $z_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i/s)$ and $t=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sum_i z_i^2)$ by sequential rounded operations, then $\\widehat r=\\operatorname{fl}(s\\operatorname{fl}(\\sqrt t))$. Set $\\sigma=1$ when $x_1=0$ and $\\sigma=\\operatorname{sign}(x_1)$ otherwise, $\\widehat\\alpha=-\\sigma\\widehat r$, $v_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i-\\widehat\\alpha\\,1_{i=1})$, $w=\\operatorname{fl}(v^Tv)$, and $\\widehat\\tau=\\operatorname{fl}(2/w)$. Compute $d=\\operatorname{fl}(v^TB)$ by sequential rounded products and additions, $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$, $U_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(p_i d_j)$, and $\\widehat B_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(B_{ij}-U_{ij})$. The complete active output is $C_+=[\\widehat\\alpha e_1\\;\\widehat B]$: write exact zeros below its first diagonal entry. This fixes the multiplication order and includes the column overwrite in the analyzed step. Return the first range failure on any invalid or out-of-range operation; return failure if $t$, $\\widehat r$, or $w$ is not positive normal, or any intermediate is nonfinite. Otherwise return $(v,\\widehat\\tau,\\widehat\\alpha,C_+)$. Store these reflectors to represent the exact orthogonal product; a rounded explicit dense product is a separate output with its own arithmetic error. The exact reflector associated with nonzero stored $v$ is $H(v)=I-2vv^T/(v^Tv)$, using [[def-householder-reflector]] and the QR convention of [[def-full-reduced-and-column-pivoted-computational-qr-factorisations]]. This definition does not assert a local backward-error bound.",
