-          "fact": "F4",
-          "source": "alg-complex-scaled-householder-reflector-step",
-          "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "For a stored complex column $x\\in\\mathbb C^m$, $m\\ge1$, and block $B\\in\\mathbb C^{m\\times q}$, $q\\ge0$, call the Householder branch of [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]] on $[x\\;B]$. This is the canonical scaled real-component norm and separately scaled phase-modulus realization, with fixed sequential dots, real-coefficient multiplication, complex product and subtraction order. It includes the exact target-column overwrite. Return its $(v,\\widehat\\tau,\\widehat\\alpha,\\widehat x,\\widehat B)$ on success; a zero column returns identity, zero column and copied $B$. Report an invalid/nonpositive stored-vector norm as `breakdown`; every other invalid/out-of-range operation returns `range-failure` with its operation index and partial values.\n\nThe exact representative is $P(v)=I-2vv^*/(v^*v)$ for nonzero stored $v$. Store this product representation rather than identifying the rounded rank-one action with an exactly unitary dense matrix. For polynomial-vector initialization, form the reflector from that external vector and use its separate-block application on the entire active row panel; do not overwrite an unrelated matrix column. The proof-backed target and separate-block coefficients are supplied by [[lem-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-local-backward-error]].",
